# License

Except where a specific file, directory, or release states otherwise, this
repository contains **multiple licensing classes**, not one blanket license.
ThisIsJohnnyt licenses only the copyright and similar rights actually owned
or licensable by ThisIsJohnnyt in each class below. Third-party components
retain their own original terms regardless of anything stated here.

See [PDR-002](docs/decisions/PDR-002.md) for the full reasoning behind this
routing.

## 1. Dataset (`datasets/`)

**CC BY-NC-SA 4.0** (Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike). Full legal text:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/legalcode.en

This project's corpus is a fresh start — no dataset content carries over
from this project's predecessor, `intent-recovery-model`. As of this
repository's creation, `datasets/gold/` is empty; this license applies from
the first real content committed here forward. See
[PDR-003](docs/decisions/PDR-003.md).

## 2. Documentation (this repository's own prose: `docs/`, `README.md`,
   dataset cards, decision records, etc.)

**CC BY-NC-SA 4.0**, same terms as the dataset (Attribution, NonCommercial,
ShareAlike).

## 3. Software (training/inference code, e.g. `training/*.py`)

**PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0** — see
[`LICENSES/PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0.md`](LICENSES/PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0.md)
for the full text. Chosen over CC BY-NC-SA specifically for code: it's a
real software license (copyright grant, distribution/modification terms,
and an actual patent grant that CC licenses don't provide). See
[PDR-002](docs/decisions/PDR-002.md) for the reasoning.

PolyForm Noncommercial's attribution mechanism is a licensor-provided
`Required Notice:` line, which every recipient must receive along with the
terms (see the license text's "Notices" section). This project's Required
Notice:

> Required Notice: Intent Recovery Model v2.0 software was created by
> ThisIsJohnnyt — https://github.com/ThisIsJohnnyt/intent-recovery-model-v2

## 4. Released model weights (`intent-recovery-model-v2-*` releases)

**Not covered by an asserted copyright license.** Whether trained model
weights are copyrightable, and whether this project cleanly holds rights to
license them, is not legally settled. See
[`MODEL_RELEASE_NOTICE.md`](MODEL_RELEASE_NOTICE.md) for the full
explanation and the project's request (acknowledgment + noncommercial use —
a request, not an enforced condition). No model has been released from this
repository yet; this section applies from the first release forward. See
[`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md) for the upstream base
model (`google/flan-t5-base`, Apache 2.0) this project's releases build on.

## 5. Private data (excluded from version control)

`datasets/real_validation.jsonl` and `datasets/real_holdout.jsonl` are not
licensed at all — excluded from version control, intended to contain the
project owner's real personal notes, never published.

## Why not "open source"

A NonCommercial restriction is incompatible with the Open Source
Initiative's Open Source Definition (criterion 6: no discrimination against
fields of endeavor). This project is precisely described as
**source-available/noncommercial**, not OSI "open source."

## GitHub license detection

GitHub's automatic license detector does not reliably recognize
CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0. PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0 is a real SPDX-listed license,
but detector support isn't guaranteed. Either way, this doesn't affect legal
validity — each linked file's actual text is what governs, regardless of
what the repository sidebar shows.
